# Duplicate inFlightRef between useFollowMutation and FollowButton

## Problem Statement

Both the hook (`useFollow.ts:51`) and component (`FollowButton.tsx:20`) own separate `inFlightRef` guards. They don't coordinate. Unmount/remount can strand the hook-level ref as `true`, preventing further mutations.

**Agent consensus: 2/8** (Simplicity, TypeScript)

## Fix

Remove `inFlightRef` from `FollowButton`. Rely on `disabled={isCheckingFollow || isMutating}` which is sufficient. The hook-level ref can also be removed if there's only one consumer — `isPending` from React Query is the authoritative guard.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Single guard mechanism (not two redundant refs)
- [ ] Follow/unfollow still prevented during pending mutation
